y":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"We might want to tune the \"passive\" flags a bit more, as the ORM insists on loading this m2o when it's not necessary.  disabling a load for that part overall fails on the test_cycles tests.    if we can figure out how to discern between these two cases that would help.\r\n```python\r\n\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import ForeignKey\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Integer\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import String\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.declarative import declarative_base\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import backref\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import relationship\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import Session\r\n\r\nBase = declarative_base()\r\n\r\n\r\nclass A(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"a\"\r\n\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    email = Column(String, unique=True)\r\n\r\n    bs = relationship(\r\n        \"B\",\r\n        # same with raise_on_sql\r\n        backref=backref(\"user\", lazy=\"raise\"),\r\n        primaryjoin=\"A.email == B.email\",\r\n    )\r\n\r\n\r\nclass B(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"b\"\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    email = Column(String, ForeignKey(\"a.email\"))\r\n\r\n\r\ne = create_engine(\"sqlite://\", echo=True)\r\nBase.metadata.create_all(e)\r\n\r\ns = Session(e)\r\n\r\nu1 = A(email=\"x\", bs=[B()])\r\ns.add(u1)\r\n\r\ns.commit()\r\n\r\n\r\ne1 = s.query(B).first()\r\ns.delete(e1)\r\ns.flush()\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nreferences #5983 ","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","s